# the string type is declared *in the program*, so the stdlib's own must be out of the way - two
# `#[core: string]` declarations in one program is a located error. that is not a workaround, it
# is the claim: the compiler binds the type by the attribute and never by the name, so a program
# may declare its own and everything below still holds
stdlib: off

--- OUT --->
3
2
--- IR --->
# the cost model, which is the whole reason `string::view` is a public type: handing a `string` to a
# view parameter touches no reference count, while handing it by value takes exactly one retain

CHECK: define i32 @main(

# the literal, as ever, a constant
CHECK: store %string { %view { ptr @str, i64 3 }, ptr null }

# show(string::view) - the conversion is a call to the `#[implicit]` method the type declared, taking
# the address of the place. the view is a two-word aggregate so it comes back through sret, then
# travels into `show` as a first-class argument
CHECK: call void @_M6string_viewZZMRBMLC6string(ptr noalias sret(%view.0)
CHECK: call void @_showZZMLCN6string4viewE

# ...and no reference count moved to get there. this is the claim that would silently regress if the
# declared conversion ever went through the copy path
CHECK-NOT: strong.inc

# which(string) - by value, so this one *does* go through the synthesized copy, whose body holds the
# retain. the two calls sitting next to each other is the contrast worth pinning
#
# the `C` before `LC6string` is the parameter's pointee being **const**: a synthesized copy takes
# `const Foo&` wherever its properties allow one (AST::copy_source_may_be_const), and a string's are a
# view and a class handle, neither of which needs to write through the source
#
# a `string` is three words and a `view` is two; both are aggregates, so both answers go through
# sret. that is return_abi_for's line - size is not the question. the contrast worth pinning is
# still the retain, not the signature
#
# **the `sret` is checked on the *call* and not only on the definition**, which is the bug this spelling
# exists to catch: LLVM will fall back to the callee's attributes when a call site omits it, right up
# until a merge leaves the two units naming two `%string`s - and then the hidden pointer travels in the
# wrong register and every argument shifts one along
CHECK: call void @_stringZZMRBCLC6string(ptr noalias sret(%string) align 8 %call.sret
CHECK: call void @_whichZZMLC6string

CHECK: ret i32 0
